{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>But on the tenth of the month.</b> 'But' is a term of restriction. All the festivals are called 'sacred proclamations' in eating and drinking and clothing and delight; only this one is called a sacred proclamation in affliction of soul. <b>And you shall afflict your souls</b> — because in the first tablets it is written, 'they saw Elohim and ate and drank,' and from excess of eating and drinking they bowed down to the calf. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded to fast on the day on which the latter tablets were given, which is Yom HaKippurim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:41.694726656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}